        "supportProgression": [
          "Stage 1 - Name the three quantities: with every value shown in a festival equal-groups situation, the learner labels number of groups, size of each group, and total. No computation is asked for and none is needed (item lmc-c-01).",
          "Stage 2 - Locate the unknown: one quantity is missing and the learner names which one it is, still without computing. Record whether the learner computes unprompted (item lmc-c-02).",
          "Stage 3 - Match operation to the named unknown: total unknown means multiply the two knowns; a missing factor means find the number that reaches the known total. The learner states the choice before computing (items lmc-c-03, lmc-c-04).",
          "Stage 4 - Solve missing factors: missing-factor equations and equal-sharing group size, factors 3-9 and products to 56, using a known fact or division (items lmc-c-03, lmc-c-04).",
          "Stage 5 - Discriminate under interleaving: total-unknown and factor-unknown items in mixed order, with divide-when-total-unknown coded separately from computation slips (item lmc-c-05).",
          "Stage 6 - Multiple factor pairs for a known total: the learner produces two or more distinct valid equal-row arrays and states that more than one correct arrangement exists; record whether the second pair arrived before or after a keep-going prompt (item lmc-c-06).",
          "Stage 7 - Independent transfer: an unassisted mixed festival set covering all in-scope item types, with the unknown named before each solution (item lmc-c-07).",
          "Support fading: modeled naming at Stages 1-2, a single keep-going or which-quantity-is-missing prompt at Stages 3-6, and no prompting at Stage 7. Assistance level is recorded on every item so that unassisted accuracy is never inferred from assisted work.",
          "Presentation is varied across items without asserting any format preference for this learner; format is recorded as an activity-level fact only."
        ],
        "charterConcern": "Single concern, raised without altering the charter: the charter's evidence requirements ask for a matched comparison of naming-the-unknown versus additional undifferentiated practice (to test dec-002, confidence 0.65), but every item in this packet embeds the naming step, so this packet alone cannot produce that contrast. Every item will yield unknown_position.named.correct.rate and error.multiply_the_given_numbers.rate.after_naming, yet with no no-naming comparison set the effect of naming remains confounded with practice and with ordering. I have also recorded latency on each item so the charter's naming-adds-cost-without-benefit check is at least measurable. If the pipeline wants dec-002 tested rather than assumed, a matched companion set at equivalent difficulty without the naming field would need to be authored downstream; that decision sits outside my authority and I have not adjusted the charter, scope, or progression to accommodate it."
